{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the recommendation failures and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200.\n\n**Cause:** The `recommendation` Service had `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. That setting only routes traffic to pods on the same node. The recommendation pod runs on `kind-worker`, so calls from the frontend on other nodes timed out. `/api/recommendations` took 10–15 seconds and then returned 500.\n\n**Fix:** I patched the Service back to `internalTrafficPolicy: Cluster`:\n\n`kubectl patch svc recommendation -n astronomy-shop -p '{\"spec\":{\"internalTrafficPolicy\":\"Cluster\"}}'`\n\n**Check:** `/api/recommendations` now returns 200 in about 0.08 seconds.\n\n**Left alone:**\n- `otel-collector` also has `internalTrafficPolicy: Local`. It looks like the intended setup for a per-node collector agent, and I didn't touch it.\n- `/api/shipping` returned 500 in my probe, but that was my malformed test request (the frontend log showed a JSON parse error on the input)."}}
